Vaccines go through extensive clinical trials involving thousands of participants to ensure safety and efficacy before they are approved for public use.
Regulatory bodies such as the FDA and WHO enforce strict guidelines and continuous monitoring to ensure vaccines remain safe and effective over time.
Adverse reactions to vaccines are rare, and extensive post-market surveillance systems are in place to detect and address any safety concerns promptly.
The same rigorous testing standards applied to vaccines are used for other medications, ensuring a high level of safety across the board.
The benefits of vaccination in preventing diseases far outweigh the risks, as evidenced by the significant reduction in disease incidence worldwide.